WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:04.889
A decimal shows parts of a whole, just like a fraction.

00:05.339 --> 00:11.190
Cut a whole into ten equal parts. Each part is one tenth, or zero point one.

00:11.640 --> 00:16.656
Shade three parts. That is three tenths, or zero point three.

00:17.106 --> 00:24.141
The digit after the decimal point is in the tenths place. So zero point three means three tenths.

00:24.591 --> 00:30.582
On a number line, zero point three sits three tenths of the way from zero to one.
